    "result_text": "All 265 tests pass, including the two new acceptance tests. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` derived field on the owner API, formatted `<TIER>_<AREA>`:\n- **TIER** = `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel >= 3`, else `STANDARD`\n- **AREA** = `METRO` when the locality is a known region (NSW, VIC, QLD), else `REGIONAL`\n\nChanges made, following the existing derived-field conventions in this codebase:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `ownerSegment` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerSegment.java`** (new) \u2014 A small helper computing the segment from `membershipLevel` + `locality`, kept out of `OwnerMapper` like the other `MembershipPoints`/`OwnerLocality`/`AgeBand` helpers so MapStruct doesn't treat it as an implicit mapping.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"ownerSegment\", ignore = true)`, since (like `membershipLevel`) it's populated by the controller once the level is known.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 `applyMembership(...)` now also sets `ownerSegment` via a new `applyOwnerSegment` helper, and `addOwner` re-applies it after `capMembershipLevelToHousehold` so the segment reflects the final (possibly capped) level.\n\n5. **`OwnerRestControllerV2.java`** \u2014 The page-listing `applyMembership` sets `ownerSegment` per DTO as well.\n\nThe two acceptance tests (`STANDARD_METRO` for a known NSW region, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown region) pass, and the full suite (265 tests) is green.",
